    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33996" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμβῐ-όω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Her.</u>
					2.3
				</span></i>
			:—<i>live in</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν νήσῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					5.19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς Ἀθήναις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Or.</u>
					18.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πέντε . . ἡγεμονίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Galb.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πολιτικαῖς πράξεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.789a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of plants,
				<i>become established</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.6.4
			</span></i>; simply, <i>take root</i>, ib. <i><span class="en">
				6.7.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ γῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.</div>
